# Content internal linking (publish checklist)

Educational URLs pass one crawlable link **up** to the matching service page, then `/contact`. Do not mesh pages together. Do not invent routes or change slugs in this pass.

Destinations that already exist: `/pillar1`–`/pillar7`, `/system`, `/contact`. Visible text uses the **service name**, never “pillar N”.

## Blog

- One in-body link to the matching service page (anchor is the service name).
- Soft `/contact` (PostEndCTA already points there).
- Optional one extra: matching book hub **or** one sibling post. Not both.
- Paste the **live** slug. After a slug rename, search published `body[].markDefs` hrefs for the old path the same day.

## Toolkit

- Fill `internalLinkDestination` on the item (service page).
- Do not add links from one tool page to another.

## Guides

- `ctaLink` is `https://sysbilt.com/contact` (or `/contact`).
- Do not rewrite `/guides/dashboards` copy unless asked.

## Same-site hrefs

Keep `https://sysbilt.com/...` or a root-relative path. Same-site links stay on-site in the renderer (no `target="_blank"`). External citations still open in a new tab.
